  "review_fixes": [
    "Wi-Fi: B5qAth11kCompat device_get_mac_address now calls board nw_board_mac() instead of returning a local random address; generated WifiNet adds ifnet bind flags/eflags/cap/lladdr/GMAC and bounded 64-frame/24-per-direction ARP/DHCP probes, RX flush and input stall counters.",
    "USB: IR1/IR2 have no GIC SPI; QcomDwc3::deliverSecondary() delivers through the filter under the existing IRQ lock without gIrqWindow storm accounting. A 1ms/50ms backoff bridge snapshots IMAN/ERDP, preserves the 427-slot XHCI ABI, and is joined before host teardown. Enumeration/child-service probes are bounded.",
    "DisplayPort: AuxPins success now follows the latched CFG/OUT value, while GPIO180 IN bit0 is diagnostic (inMismatch). Failed CFG/OUT restores the mux and clears owned. Link probes cover hardware open, AUX dump, EDID/fitting modes, DPCD 0x202..0x207, training, DPU resources, scanout failure stage and the first three presents.",
    "Tests: new ASan/UBSan Review16 gate and wrapper; DP board test models latch success, IN mismatch, rollback and restore; 26 DP test files retained; pre-ci runs Review16 after Review15."
  ],
  "first_errors": [
    "Wi-Fi target initially could not find xcrun/brew in this Linux host; rerun with tools/llvm21 and explicit libLLVM path.",
    "QcomDwc3 first compile rejected void hostIrqBridge(void*) because kernel_thread_start requires thread_continue_t(void*,int); signature corrected.",
    "WifiNet first target compile rejected KERNEL_PRIVATE ifnet_eflags absent from the public SDK; generated C++ now declares the pinned XNU KPI explicitly.",
    "The initial DP board test modeled IN bit0 without a shift and expected old IN-based failure; test now models CFG/OUT latch success plus diagnostic IN mismatch.",
    "First full local gate stopped at wifi-diagnostics because the Review16 stall probe added ifnet_name/eflags/capabilities and errors_in/dropped fields absent from that old mock; mock fields were added and the complete chain was rerun."
  ],
